; GrassClover — Grass terrain dressing (open_grass), variant 3 of 4: lawn with clover through
; it. NEW in the 2026-09-08 grass-family rework.
;
; 26x Grass_Common_Short at 0.075 + 14x Clover_1 at 0.0699 (raw AABB height 1.144732 -> 0.080
; tile-units) + 10x Clover_2 at 0.0633 (raw 1.263785 -> 0.080), seed 20260909. Both clover
; scales are NEW FIRST-PASS PROPOSALS — no GDD number exists for clover height. They sit
; deliberately BELOW the 0.100 grass baseline: clover is a low broad-leaved ground cover that
; grows through grass rather than above it, so a clover reading taller than the blades around
; it would look wrong even at a "correct" measured height.
;
; CLOVER IS IN GRASS ON A HUMAN RULING (2026-09-08): "some clover would be good in grass, that
; happens in nature."
;
; NO FLOWERS HERE, AND THAT IS A DESIGN RULE RATHER THAN AN OVERSIGHT. The grass family's prop
; vocabulary is partitioned by the habitat tags each terrain emits, so the visual and the tag
; agree — the idiom Meadow.tscn's header already states for itself. Grass emits `open_grass`
; ALONE; Meadow emits `open_grass` + `flowers` and is the only source of that tag. Scattering
; single flowers here would look fine and would quietly make the two terrains hard to tell
; apart, which matters because a player reads habitat off the ground. Clover clears this rule
; because it reads as leaf ground-cover, not bloom.
;
; BUILT BY A ONE-OFF HEADLESS SCRIPT, NOT HAND-AUTHORED, AND NOT EDITABLE BY HAND. MultiMesh's
; per-instance transform buffer is a flat PackedFloat32Array in a 12-floats-per-instance
; layout, and the blade mesh is lifted out of its imported .gltf and embedded here; both are
; cases this codebase has always built with the engine rather than by hand (see this file's
; own history). Re-run the generator to change anything below, do not edit the buffer.
;
; HEADLESS CAVEAT, re-confirmed 2026-09-08: Godot's dummy RenderingServer does not implement
; MultiMesh.set_instance_transform(), so the generator writes `buffer` directly, row-major 3x4
; per instance: [bx.x, by.x, bz.x, o.x, bx.y, by.y, bz.y, o.y, bx.z, by.z, bz.z, o.z]. The
; layout was verified against the previously shipped GrassCommonShort buffer before use.
;
; SHARED FAMILY BASELINE (identical in all four Grass variants, so they read as one terrain):
; slab BoxMesh 1.0 x 0.2 x 1.0 at y=-0.1 in Color(0.42, 0.68, 0.3) — the 1.0 width is the
; established cross-tile seam-gap fix, do not narrow it; 2 blotchy floor patches (dark
; Color(0.34, 0.58, 0.22), light Color(0.52, 0.74, 0.32)) at y=0.001, the standing workaround
; for "no tileable ground texture exists in the audited packs" (MegaKit's Grass.png is a thin
; UV-strip palette texture for vertex-style mesh colouring, not a tiling ground texture).
; Scatter is a fixed-seed deterministic pass within +/-0.42 tile-units of centre, which keeps
; every instance inside the 1.0 slab and out of the neighbouring tile.
;
; EVERYTHING GROUND-LEVEL NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" — the OcclusionFader exemption
; convention; see CommonTree1.tscn's header for the mechanism.
;
; ALL COLOURS, COUNTS AND SCALES ARE FIRST-PASS PROPOSALS AWAITING HUMAN SIGN-OFF. This variant
; set is the CALIBRATION REFERENCE for the wider grass-family rework (human ruling 2026-09-08:
; "calibrate on Grass first"): once these values are ruled on, they become the house baseline
; applied to Meadow, Scrub and Wild grass rather than being re-proposed per terrain.
;
; Source: Stylized Nature MegaKit (Standard/free), Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — License.txt
; re-checked per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate before this pass. See
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_stylized_nature_megakit.tres.
;
; GRASS COLOUR: TRUE GREEN BAND (2026-09-08, human-reported "the grass is very yellow").
; Grass.png is a 4-band vertical palette strip, each band 28px of a 512px texture, and the
; colour of every blade in this project comes from WHICH BAND its UVs land in — nothing tints
; anything (albedo is pure white, no vertex colours). The bands are:
;   band 1  x 0-27    rgb(177,152,0)  gold
;   band 2  x 28-55   rgb(57,149,0)   TRUE GREEN
;   band 3  x 56-83   rgb(185,87,0)   rust
;   band 4  x 84-111  rgb(103,163,0)  yellow-green
; Band 2 was the one band NOTHING in the project sampled: the Wispy meshes ship on band 1
; (gold) and the Common meshes on band 4 (yellow-green), which is why the world read warm.
; `uv1_offset` below re-centres this material's UV span in band 2, computed per mesh from its
; own measured span so every one lands with ~7px of margin on both band edges (mip bleed).
; The MESH IS UNTOUCHED — this is a material property and is reversible by deleting one line.
;
; OCCLUSIONFADER REMOVED 2026-09-08 — ANY MENTION OF IT BELOW IS HISTORY. The per-resident
; transparency fade (D-41 §4) flickered in play and was cut outright; the script, its scene node
; and its two suites are gone. The "Slab" node stays, because every terrain scene is built
; around it and removing it would restructure all 33 for no gain — but NO CODE LOOKS THAT NAME
; UP ANY MORE. It is a grouping convention now, with no behaviour attached, so nothing breaks if
; a new scene groups differently and nothing is gained by "restoring" the exemption.
[gd_scene format=4]

